$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure B for the stereoselective cross-coupling of
enolphosphates 1b and 4a-d with arylboronic acid. Toluene (4mL/mmol) and
2 M aqueous potassium phosphate (1.4 mL/mmol or 1.8 mL/mmol) was added to
a mixture of phosphate dibromide 1a,b,4a-d (1.0 eq.), boronic acid (1.4
eq . or 1.8 eq.), palladium acetate (0.02 eq., 2 mol %),
triphenylphosphine (0.06 eq., 6 mol %). The resultant mixture was stirred
at 45 °C. Then the crude reaction mixture was diluted with ether, washed
with 1M KOH, water and brine. Organic layer was dried over MgSO4,
concentrated under reduce pressure and purification by column
chromatography afforded the pure product.
(Z)-(1-Bromo-1-phenylhexene-2-yl)(diethyl) phosphate (Z)- 3b. The title
compound was prepared according the general procedure B starting from 1b
(3.940 g, 10 mmol), phenylboronic acid (1.70 g, 14 mmol), palladium
acetate (0.045 g, 0.2 mmol, 2 mol %), triphenylphosphine (0.157 g, 0.6
mmol, 6 mol %), 2M aq. K3PO4 (14 mL), and toluene (40 mL). The reaction
mixture was stirred 8 h at 45 °C, following column chromatography (silica
gel, EtOAc-hexane 1:3, UV detection). 3.480 g (89%) of the title product
as a yellowish oil. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.77 (t, J = 6.8 Hz,
3H), 1.20 (m, 2H), 1.38 (dt, J = 7.6 Hz, J (P-H) = 1.1 Hz, 6H), 1.52 (m,
2H), 2.36 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, J (P-H) = 1.4 Hz, 2H), 4.27 (dq, J = 7.3 Hz, J
(P-H) = 7.2 Hz, 4H), 7.29-7.34 (m, 5H). 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
13.58, 16.09 (d, J (C-P) = 7.2 Hz), 21.84, 29.03, 31.23, 64.56 (d, J
(C-P) = 6.2 Hz), 108.40 (d, J (C-P) = 10.0 Hz), 128.32, 128.50, 129.51
(d, J (C-P) = 1.8 Hz), 137.70, 148.19 (d, J (C-P) = 7.5 Hz). HRMS (APCI):
Calc. for C16H24BrO4P+H+ [M+H+]: 391.0668; Found: 391.0674. Rf = 0.35.
