$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure (Table 1):
2(Z)-2-amino-3-bromo-3-phenyl-2-propenoic acid (1 equiv) or
2(E)-2-amino-3-bromo-3-phenyl-2-propenoic acid, arylboronic acid (1
equiv), potassium phospate tribasic monohydrate (2 equiv),
2-dicyclohexylphophino-2'-(N,N-dimethylamino)biphenyl (13 mol%) and
palladium acetate (13 mol%) were mixted together into a seal tube.
Degassed water (1.0 ml) and degassed THF (4.6 ml) were added. The mixture
was degassed again and heated 2 hours at 70 °C. The reaction mixture was
diluted with NaHCO3 sat. (10 mL/g) and extracted with EtOAc (3x15 mL/g).
The combined organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4. The solvent was
removed under reduced pressure and the crude mixture purified by column
chromatography on silica gel to provide products.
(Z)-2-Acetylamino-3-(4-fluoro-phenyl)-3-phenyl-acrylic acid methyl ester
(2c). The general procedure was followed. Isolated 384 mg (73%). ¹H NMR
(400 MHz, CHCl3-d): δ 7.44-7.38 (3 H, m), 7.36-7.29 (2 H, m) 7.25-7.14
(m, 4 H), 6.91-6.80 (m, 1 H), 3.64 (s, 3 H), 2.14 (s, 3 H); 13C NMR (100
MHz, CHCl3-d): δ 168.8, 166.5, 163.9, 161.5, 139.1, 135.5, 134.4, 131.8,
131.8, 129.1, 128.3, 128.3, 116.1, 115.9, 52.2, 22.8; HRMS ESI (m/z): [M
+ Na]+ calcd for C18H16FNNaO3, 336.10064; found 336.10105
